#basePath P2_Outreach
#include "Header.leaf"

:: Start
@exposed
@trigger    OnLocationChanged
// "NONE" ensures no other threads are in-progress
// global:currentPhase == 2 ensures player is in phase 2
@when       global:currentThread == "NONE", global:currentPhase == 2, location == "ArmyCorps"
@cutscene
// Lock all location on map
$call SetInThreadLocks()
$call DisableMapButton()

// Mark start of thread
$set global:currentThread = "P2_Outreach"

{@}   
       You park your car on the side of the road, the Army Corps of Engineers building up ahead.
       In it's shade, you have a sudden memory of being here for a high school field trip. 
       At the time, Janie had said she could see herself in the Corps. 
       You find her number quickly on your phone and call her.

{@You}
       Hey Janie! How are things going in New York?

{@Janie}
       </i>Oh, you know how it is. My manager doesn't believe in personal time or on-call pay.</i> 

{@You}
       That sucks a lot. 
       So, random question, but do you remember when we visited the Army Corps of Engineers in high school?

{@Janie}
       </i>Uhhh, maybe. Oh wait, yes I do.</i>

{@You}
       Think you'd ever wanna come back? Maybe join up?

{@}
       There's a pause from the other end of the line. 

{@Janie}
       </i>Probably not. I mean, I've got the whole world at my fingertips here.</i>
       </i>Why would I want to go back to the middle of nowhere?</i>

{@You}
       I'm back in the middle of nowhere.

{@Janie}
       </i>Ana, come on, you know what I mean. </i>
       </i>Look, I'm sorry. I gotta go. I'll call you later, okay?</i>

{@}
       The call disconnects. You sit for a moment in your car, gnawing at your lip. 
       Then you throw your phone back into your pocket and step out. 
       You notice an engineer working on a trap outside the building and flag them down. 

{@You}
       Hello. Sorry to interrupt, but could I ask you some questions? 

{@}
       The engineer stands up and nods warmly. 
       You notice the surname "Robertson" embroidered on their high-visibility vest. 

{@Robertson}
       Yes, of course. Thanks for stopping by.
       No one ever really comes to visit us. 

{@You}
       You're quite a ways away from everything. 

{@Robertson}
       What can I say? We love the brush. 
       So, what can I help you with, ma'am?

{@You}
       I had some questions about sea lamprey management. 
       You were pretty involved in previous management efforts, right?

{@Robertson}
       Yes, ma'am. We were very involved. 
       We built traps, barriers, helped coordinate lampricide application. The whole works.
       I also sterilized some adult sea lamprey. 
{@You}
       And these were successful?

{@Robertson}
       Yes, ma'am, they were. We helped reduce the population by 90%. 
       Nothin' if not efficient. //receive evidence chip
       Hasn't been so much work done lately, but we're always ready to restart. 

{@You}
       Well, I've been tasked with creating an intervention plan for managing sea lamprey populations. 
       You wouldn't happen to have any advice for me?

{@Robertson}
       'Course I do, ma'am. 
       All those things I mentioned earlier - barriers, traps, the like - restarting 'em will help. 
       In the meantime, though, getting the locals onboard will help lots. 
       If they can tell us where they are seeing bites, that can help us identify tributaries to target. 

{@You}
       That can be done. I know some people down at the docks. 

{@Robertson}
       Don't we all. 
       Well, don't be a stranger, ma'am. Come back when you want yer traps. 

{@You}
       Don't worry. I will. 

{@}
       By the time you get back to your car, your previous phone call is almost forgotten. 

// TODO: Rest of Army Corps section here

// TODO: Give evidence chip
// $call GiveEvidenceChip([Evidence])

$call UnlockLocation(FishingDocks)
$call EnableMapButton()


:: AtFishingDocks
@trigger    OnLocationChanged
// global:currentThread ensures the correct thread
// global:currentPhase == 2 ensures player is in phase 2
@when       global:currentThread == "P2_Outreach", global:currentPhase == 2, location == "FishingDocks"
// Lock all location on map
$call SetInThreadLocks()
$call DisableMapButton()

{@}   
       When you were a kid, you always found the sound of the water lapping at the dock soothing. 
       You're pleased to see it's still soothing now, all these years later. 

{@João}
       Ana, querida. It's good to see you. 

{@}
       You look up to see your uncles heading your way, quickly enveloping you in a warm hug. 

{@You}
       It's good to see you, too, Tio João, Tio Renato. 
       How've things been?

{@Renato}
       Well, you know how it is. Good tides, bad tides. 

{@You}
       Lakes don't have meaningful tides. 

{@}
       He waves at you as if to say, "You know what I mean."
       You look around the dock and notice its newfound emptiness. 

{@You}
       Where's everyone else?

{@João}
       Ah. 
       Johnny and Rick retired a few years, Lana moved away, the rental place closed...

{@Renato}
       The kids left for college and didn't come back. 
       Except for you, of course. 

{@}
       He ruffles your hair. 
       Up close you can see wrinkles on his face that you don't remember being there. 

{@You}
       Anyway, um, I've actually come to ask for your help. 

{@João}
       Claro, querida. Whatever you need. 

{@You}
       You've been seeing more lamprey bites on your fish, right?

{@Renato}
       We have, yes. 

{@João}
       Some of the others have seen bites too.

{@You}
       As part of my work, I'm trying to get more information on where fishers are seeing these bites. 
       I'm starting a program where fishers can call in to a number at my work if they see sea lamprey bites.
       Would you be willing to spread this information to the others?

{@Renato}
       Definitely. We'll ask them to spread the numbers around, too. 

{@João}
       This is our livelihood. It's in our best interest, too, to help, too. 

{@You}
       Obrigada! It really means a lot to me. 

{@}
       You hand them a stack of fliers with the number for your office. 

{@Renato}
       We'll make sure these go where they need to go. 
       //action card
       Want to join us on the boat for a bit? Have a Guaraná?

{@You}
       I'm sorry, I can't. I have so much to do. 
       But what about after I'm done? 

{@João}
       That works. We'll celebrate out on the water like when you were a kid. 

{@}
       They ruffle your hair. It feels nice to feel little again. 
// TODO: Rest of Town Hall section here

// TODO: Give action card
// $call GiveActionCard([Action])


// TEMPORARY: skip to end
$goto .End


:: End
@exposed
@tracked
// Unlock next locations
$call UnlockLocation(FieldStationLampricide)     // P2_Lampricide

// Mark end of thread
$set global:currentThread = "NONE"

// Go to Phase 2 Continue Hub
$goto P2_Hub.Continue